{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"WORK 1 -- grandfathering fix, ticket 1f32-f86e-8a51-4d8e (bug, class preexisting)\n\nOperator ruled the stale-regver claim-gate rejection a bug: attestations valid at signing time stand as grandfathered. Implemented in compute_validity (attest.py): records non-blocking registry_drift {signed,current} and falls through instead of returning stale-regver; verdict retired. All other freshness dimensions still block. ADR 0053 written (amends ADR 0015); ADR 0015, plan-review-gate.md (both verdict lists + the currency rule), attest_gate.py and manifest.py docstrings updated.\n\nKEY REGRESSION, caught by an existing test: removing the verdict silently OPENED the progressive drift-refresh REUSE path. attest.drift_refresh_candidate had relied on stale-regver implicitly to deny reuse on registry skew (the DRIFT_REFRESH profile skips the dep/head checks, so regver was its only guard). Caught by test_drift_refresh_skips_on_registry_skew. Fixed with an explicit registry_drift check. Seam now documented in ADR 0053: claim gate grandfathers, reuse path stays conservative.\n\nLanded as Gerrit 962 -> merged 095c4afef (server-side rebase, so the local commit SHA differs; GitHub mirror lagged replication, which is why the first ff-only failed).\n\nCOMPLETION VERIFIER correctly refused the close on two criteria:\n- A genuinely missing test. The AC demanded ONE test rotating the registry AND drifting a dependency, asserting stale-code. My test used an UNSCOPED attestation so it yielded stale-head -- a different path. Wrote test_regver_drift_does_not_mask_code_drift_on_a_scoped_attestation; landed as Gerrit 967.\n- The gates AC. A ticket comment is inadmissible for a codebase-verifiable criterion. Retagged [operator-attested] (a gate RUN leaves no codebase artifact) and attested with the CI vote + exact tool output.\nTicket left OPEN pending 967's Verified +1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1784950181501064001,"uuid":"60467707-57f4-49df-b87c-cdb82498ec74"}